    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced. The bull case rests on a confirmed uptrend (price above 10 EMA, 50 SMA, 200 SMA, golden cross, +17.12% over 60 days) and a strong balance sheet from the FY2023 10-K ($327.9B equity, $55B net cash generation, $25.6B returned to shareholders). However, the bear case is equally compelling on technical extension: RSI at 72.92 with repeated 80 peaks in March, price hugging the upper Bollinger Band at $191.03, and a 9.7% gap above the 50 SMA. Critically, the income statement, news flow, and macro data are all unavailable as of March 28, 2024, meaning there is no fundamental confirmation of earnings growth to justify chasing at the top of the range. The prudent stance is to maintain current exposure without adding at these extended levels, and to be ready to add on a pullback toward the 10 EMA ($185.94) or 50 SMA ($173.30) where risk/reward improves meaningfully.\n\n**Entry Price**: 185.94\n\n**Stop Loss**: 173.3\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-slightly-constructive weight; avoid overweighting until a pullback provides a better entry or fundamental confirmation arrives via an income statement/earnings report.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
